 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Why did one hungry sailor eat a breakfast worth a whole house?",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.071
  },
  {
   "text": "He bites into an onion with his fish, and a merchant starts screaming.",
   "s": 3.371,
   "e": 6.601
  },
  {
   "text": "So the sailor grabs his plate and runs, still chewing.",
   "s": 6.801,
   "e": 9.243
  },
  {
   "text": "The merchant chases him through the harbor, past ships and fish carts.",
   "s": 9.443,
   "e": 12.561
  },
  {
   "text": "Sailors laugh. Who chases a man over half an onion?",
   "s": 12.761,
   "e": 15.401
  },
  {
   "text": "But the merchant brings the whole street. A baker, a fishwife, even a dog.",
   "s": 15.701,
   "e": 19.405
  },
  {
   "text": "They corner him at the end of the dock, and he swallows the last bite!",
   "s": 19.605,
   "e": 22.308
  },
  {
   "text": "So what was so special about that onion?",
   "s": 22.508,
   "e": 24.198
  },
  {
   "text": "That onion was a tulip bulb, and that winter, Holland went crazy for tulips.",
   "s": 24.498,
   "e": 28.48
  },
  {
   "text": "One rare bulb could buy a house, a horse, and a year of bread.",
   "s": 28.68,
   "e": 31.424
  },
  {
   "text": "People traded whole farms for flowers they had never even seen.",
   "s": 31.624,
   "e": 34.97
  },
  {
   "text": "So the sailor had eaten the priciest breakfast in town.",
   "s": 35.37,
   "e": 37.882
  },
  {
   "text": "But a few weeks later, tulip prices crashed overnight.",
   "s": 38.082,
   "e": 40.86
  },
  {
   "text": "He ate a house that was about to be worth an onion.",
   "s": 41.06,
   "e": 43.277
  }
 ],
